  "ownership": [
    "BuiltinTargetRoutes owns platform admission; FullLLVMBackend validates little-endian, 32-bit x86, requested object format and relocatable output.",
    "ABI32 owns platform calling/return rules; MicrosoftStructLayout owns Microsoft C record layout, reused by IR emission.",
    "Tree size and target BitInt maximum alignment own wide integer storage, constants and scalar/variadic loads.",
    "LLVM DAG/FastISel count actual callee-popped bytes separately from caller alignment padding; Clang va_arg classifies unnamed records/vectors consistently with calls."
  ],
  "diagnostic_history": [
    "Reference and mixed-call failures exposed Windows vector/regparm/fastcall, Microsoft bitfield layout, BitInt array stride and variadic scalar storage bugs; fixed before the final ABI matrix.",
    "Mach-O relocation-site interpretation and COFF section alignment in the test loader were repaired against actual object tables; earlier failing fixtures/logs are preserved.",
    "The first LLVM regression run lacked the llvm-readelf build alias; building that target and rerunning the affected test closed it.",
    "The new Clang regression initially used an unqualified Windows-only CHECK label on Linux. The corrected prefix passes; all six selected tests pass.",
    "The first expanded bounded run exposed the i686-apple-darwin alias bug, fixed and tested for i386/i486/i586/i686."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three DynCode struct tests are skipped because their native loader is unavailable on this Linux host.",
    "Cross-platform ABI tests execute objects in Unicorn, not Windows/Darwin OS services, SEH or integrated linking.",
    "Bounded-system and VMFUNC witnesses intercept privileged instructions. They do not qualify physical EPT switching, system effects, VM-exit/fault/event continuation or hardware completion.",
    "Vectorcall, MinGW/Android/iOS source routes, an embedded i386 machine backend and bundled i386 runtime/sysroot remain outside this route.",
    "Real/VM86/task transitions, remaining original-machine i386 banks/providers, software SMM/SGX, unbound asynchronous producers and hardware-specific qualification remain open."
  ],
